    badge: 'Communication-led and fast to test',
    title: 'Media, content and communication',
    body: 'BJMC, BA English, mass communication programmes and self-built writing or video proof. Newsroom hiring is narrow, but brand, research, content strategy and communication roles keep growing.',
    fit: 'Best for: students who write or explain well and enjoy audience feedback.',
    watch: 'Watch out: routine first-draft writing is the part AI compresses first. Position yourself on judgment and research.',
  },
  {
    badge: 'Long training arc',
    title: 'Psychology: BA or BSc, then a master\'s and registration',
    body: 'A bachelor\'s degree alone does not make you a clinical psychologist. To practise clinically you must be on the Central Rehabilitation Register under the Rehabilitation Council of India, and "counsellor" is not a registered title today.',
    fit: 'Best for: patient students who enjoy behaviour, research method and long study.',
    watch: 'Watch out: ask every college which route it leads to, and never rely on the word "psychologist" in a brochure.',
  },
  {
    badge: 'Stable and structured',
    title: 'Teaching: ITEP (BA B.Ed) or BA then B.Ed',
    body: 'The 4-year ITEP through NCET combines a subject degree and teacher training. Government school pay is fixed by pay level, so growth comes from promotion and any coaching or content work you build alongside.',
    fit: 'Best for: students who enjoy explaining and want a predictable career.',
    watch: 'Watch out: pay is capped by the scale, so plan a second income skill early.',
  },
  {
    badge: 'Long odds, needs a backup skill',
    title: 'Government exams: UPSC, state PCS and SSC after a BA',
    body: 'These exams ask for a bachelor\'s degree, so a BA keeps them open. Preparation can consume years, pay follows fixed scales, and most of what you study for the exam is not marketable if you do not clear it.',
    fit: 'Best for: students who genuinely want public service and can study steadily for a long time.',
    watch: 'Watch out: build a parallel skill and a proof of work while you prepare, so an unsuccessful attempt does not leave you starting from zero.',
  },
  {
    badge: 'Uniformed service',
    title: 'Defence: NDA Army wing now, or CDS after graduation',
    body: 'A humanities student can apply to the Army wing of NDA after 12th. Training and career are fully funded, but the Maths paper and physical standards are real filters.',
    fit: 'Best for: students who are fit, disciplined and have a plan for the maths paper.',
    watch: 'Watch out: Air Force and Navy wings need Physics, Chemistry and Maths in Class 12.',
  },
  {
    badge: 'Service industry',
    title: 'Hospitality: NCHM JEE and a hotel management degree',
    body: 'Open to any stream if English is one of your subjects. Demand is real, but full-programme tuition of Rs 3 lakh to Rs 5 lakh at many institutes makes the college\'s placement record worth checking first.',
    fit: 'Best for: people-oriented students who like operations and shift work.',
    watch: 'Watch out: early pay is modest; growth comes from moving into management and specialisms.',
  },
];

const stackRows = [
  {
    path: 'Law',
    core: 'Reading, research and precise drafting',
    multiplier: 'One niche such as IP, tech and privacy, tax or competition law, plus AI-assisted research that you verify yourself',
    proof: 'A plain-English case note, a clause explainer, a moot or internship reflection with the tasks you handled',
  },
  {
    path: 'Design',
    core: 'Visual craft and observation',
    multiplier: 'User research or motion work, plus fast AI-assisted iteration you can explain',
    proof: 'Three finished projects with process notes, and one real brief for a local business or club',
  },
  {
    path: 'BA (Hons) in any humanities subject',
    core: 'Research and clear writing',
    multiplier: 'Data basics in spreadsheets, survey design, or one useful language',
    proof: 'A short research brief with a chart, and one public analysis of a live issue',
  },
  {
    path: 'Media and content',
    core: 'Writing, reporting or video storytelling',
    multiplier: 'Audience analytics and search basics',
    proof: 'Three published pieces and one distribution experiment with the result and what you learned',
  },
  {
    path: 'Psychology and teaching',
    core: 'Observation and explanation',
    multiplier: 'Research method, or curriculum and lesson design',
    proof: 'A teaching sample, or a small survey study with a written method note',
  },
];

const payRows = [
  {
    path: 'Law: top NLU',
    entry: 'NLSIU BA LLB 2026 batch reported a median of Rs 21 lakh a year and a high of Rs 65 lakh. NIRF data for earlier batches shows a median of Rs 16 lakh.',
    typical: 'Tier-1 firm first-year offers are reported at about Rs 18 to 22.5 lakh a year.',
    caution: 'A top-college outcome, not the typical one. A district-court junior may get as low as Rs 300 per appearance with no fixed monthly pay, and paralegal roles report Rs 2 to 3.5 lakh.',
  },
  {
    path: 'Design: NIFT and similar',
    entry: 'NIFT Mumbai UG in 2023 to 24: an average of Rs 5.45 lakh with a high of Rs 12 lakh.',
    typical: 'Roughly Rs 5 to 7 lakh at the strong campuses.',
    caution: 'Depends heavily on portfolio, campus and city. Some campuses report placement rates of 60 to 68%.',
  },
  {
    path: 'Teaching: government school',
    entry: 'Basic pay under the 7th Pay Commission is Rs 35,400 for a primary teacher, Rs 44,900 for a trained graduate teacher and Rs 47,600 for a post-graduate teacher, before allowances.',
    typical: 'Steady, with regular pay scale increments.',
    caution: 'Capped by the scale. Seats and eligibility tests are competitive.',
  },
  {
    path: 'Media, content, BA jobs',
    entry: 'No reliable public median exists, so treat any single figure with suspicion.',
    typical: 'Compare with the average regular salaried wage in India: about Rs 24,217 a month for men and Rs 18,353 for women in 2025 (PLFS), roughly Rs 2.9 lakh and Rs 2.2 lakh a year.',
    caution: 'Pay moves with proof of work, a niche and the employer type more than with the degree label.',
  },
];

const denominatorItems = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Who is in the denominator',
    body: 'The NLSIU 2026 figure came from a student-run placement committee. It reports 61 students placed out of 82 who took part in placement activity, from a batch of 113. A median of Rs 21 lakh describes the placed group, not the whole batch.',
    note: 'Ask any college: how many students are in the batch, how many sat for placement, how many were placed, and what the median (not the average) was.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Median, average and highest are three different numbers',
    body: 'The highest package is the one printed in brochures. The median tells you what a typical placed student got. The average is pulled up by a few very large offers.',
    note: 'When a page quotes a range like "Rs 3 to 40 lakh" without naming the college or year, treat it as noise.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'One number is not a career',
    body: 'A first-year salary tells you nothing about year five. Compare the proof, skills and options a path gives you after two or three years, not only the first offer.',
    note: 'A lower first offer with faster skill growth can beat a higher first offer with a dead end.',
  },
];

const checkpointItems = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Biology',
    body: 'Ask what kind of days give you energy: long reading, sketching, speaking, physical routine, or people contact. Law asks for years of dense reading and drafting, design for repeated rework, and defence for physical discipline.',
    note: 'If you avoid long reading now, do not choose a reading-heavy course because it sounds respected.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Context',
    body: 'Check your family\'s runway, your city, your language comfort and how many exam attempts you can afford. A drop year for CLAT costs a year of income that a BA plus skills route would already be building.',
    note: 'A plan that needs three attempts and a loan is a different plan from one that works on the first.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Market',
    body: 'Look for the real placement report of the specific college and real job listings for the role. Learn what a graduate three years out actually does, not what a brochure promises.',
    note: 'If you cannot name three real roles the course leads to, keep researching.',
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    title: 'Survival',
    body: 'Ask which part of the work AI already does. Summaries, first drafts and template layouts are under pressure. Judgment, client trust, taste and responsibility hold up better.',
    note: 'Choose the version of the path where you end up owning a decision, not only producing a draft.',
  },
];

const situationCards = [
  {
    label: 'Strong marks and a clear pull',
    title: 'You want a top route and can back it up',
    body: 'Register for CLAT before 31 October if law appeals, and sit one full timed mock before paying the fee. Apply to NID or NIFT if you already have finished creative work. In parallel, prepare a CUET score, so the year is never empty if an exam goes badly.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Average marks or a weak school signal',
    title: 'You need a route that does not depend on one exam day',
    body: 'A BA (Hons) through CUET plus one visible skill is the safer sequence. The CLAT notification sets no upper age limit, but the Bar Council\'s age cap for 5-year LLB admission is before the Supreme Court, so check before planning a late attempt from college. Aim to build one finished piece of proof every semester, such as a research brief, portfolio piece or published writing.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Confused, or pushed toward science by family',
    title: 'You have not decided and the pressure is loud',
    body: 'Take one small test per idea instead of arguing in the abstract: a CLAT mock, a design brief, a day with a working teacher, a short psychology course. Then use the results in a calm conversation at home. Changing streams after Class 12 is not the only way to keep options open.',
  },
